course: dictionary
lesson: 4253
title: Meet the grasshopper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A grasshopper is a green or brown insect with strong back legs that jump far. «Every insect has 6 legs: ants, beetles, bees, ladybirds and grasshoppers all walk on 6 legs.» So a grasshopper is an insect, and like other insects it has 6 legs.
explain: Look at the word itself. Grass and hopper are two smaller words. A hopper is something that hops, and grasshoppers live in grass and hop through it. When you meet a long word, split it into parts and see if the parts give you a clue.
explain: Grasshoppers can also make a sound. They chirp by rubbing their legs on their wings. «Grasshoppers chirp» on warm summer days, so if you hear a chirp in the grass, a grasshopper may be near.
fact: A grasshopper is an insect with 6 legs.
fact: Grasshoppers have their ears on the sides of their bellies, while crickets have tiny ear patches just below the knees of their front legs.
fact: In Oaxaca, Mexico, «chapulines» are toasted grasshoppers with lime and chilli, eaten for thousands of years and sold at markets and football games.
fact: Desert locusts are grasshoppers that, when crowded, change colour and behaviour and form swarms of billions that eat crops.
fact: About two billion people around the world eat insects, and grasshoppers are among them.
exercise: «Every insect has 6 legs: ants, beetles, bees, ladybirds and grasshoppers all walk on 6 legs.» How many legs does a grasshopper have? | 8 | 10 | *6 | 4
exercise: What are a grasshopper's strong back legs mainly used for? | To chirp | *To jump far | To swim under water | To dig holes
exercise: «Chapulines are toasted grasshoppers with lime and chilli.» Find and copy one word that tells you the grasshoppers are cooked. | grasshoppers | lime | chilli | *toasted
test: A grasshopper makes its chirping sound by rubbing what together? | Its teeth and claws | *Its legs and wings | Its eyes and mouth | Its ears and tail
test: «Desert locusts are grasshoppers that form swarms of billions that eat crops.» Why are these swarms a problem for farmers? | They chirp too loudly | *They eat the crops | They have 8 legs | They live under the sea
exam: Splitting the word grasshopper into grass and hopper, what does hopper suggest? | Something that swims | Something that flies very high | Something made of stone | *Something that hops
